# Timeline renderer

<p class="lede">
When an agent turn ends, the server summarizes the files it wrote and the commands it ran, and appends a card to the
agent's timeline. The client renders the card and a screen with every turn. This is the <code>agent-hook</code>
template.
</p>

```sh
npx --package paseo-plugin-devkit ppd create ~/code/turn-cards --template agent-hook
cd ~/code/turn-cards && npm install
npm run check && npm test
```

```text
...
PASS  client-eval      contributions: addTimelineRenderer, addScreen
...
13 passed, 0 warnings, 0 failed, 0 skipped

 Test Files  2 passed (2)
      Tests  15 passed (15)
```

<h2 id="data">The row</h2>

A plugin timeline row has a `kind`, a `version` and `data`. The client validates `data` with the same schema before
it renders, so the schema lives in `shared/`. The RPC lets the screen list every summary of an agent.

<SourceFile path="templates/agent-hook/shared/turn-summary.ts" />

<h2 id="server">The hook</h2>

`agent.turn_ended` carries the whole conversation, so the summary starts after the last user message. Files come
from the `detail.filePath` of write and edit tool calls; a file a shell command writes is not attributed by the host.

<SourceFile path="templates/agent-hook/server/summarize.ts" />

Turns without tool calls get no card. The row is appended with `paseo.agents.ref(id).timeline.append`, and kept in
memory for the RPC:

<SourceFile path="templates/agent-hook/index.server.ts" />

<h2 id="client">The card and the screen</h2>

Timeline renderers get no navigation props, so the card closes over the `client` from `contribute` to open the
screen.

<SourceFile path="templates/agent-hook/client/summary-card.tsx" />

<SourceFile path="templates/agent-hook/index.client.tsx" />

<h2 id="run">Run it with the fake agent</h2>

```sh
mkdir -p /tmp/turn-cards-ws
npx ppd daemon up --fake-agent
npx ppd install
npx ppd paseo -- run --provider fake-agent --cwd /tmp/turn-cards-ws '{"steps":[{"write":{"path":"notes.md","content":"hi"}},{"say":"done"}]}'
npx ppd paseo -- plugin logs turn-cards
npx ppd web --shot out/card.png
```

The plugin log shows the hook ran:

```text
turn summary appended for 544f3a69-ae2b-465c-af06-6d3183b8fbf9: 1 file(s), 0 command(s)
```

<Shot
  src="/shots/turn-summary-card.png"
  alt="A fake agent turn in the Paseo web UI: the Write notes.md tool call, the reply 'done', and below it the plugin's Turn summary card with '1 file changed, 0 commands run', notes.md and an All turns button."
  width={1400}
  height={900}
  caption="The card under the fake agent's turn, from ppd web. The model picker shows the fake agent's only model, Scripted."
/>

<h2 id="test">Test it</h2>

`paseo logs` does not show plugin rows; `agentTimeline` reads the canonical timeline, plugin rows included. Hooks
run asynchronously, so poll:

```ts
import { agentTimeline, pluginRows, runFakeAgentTurn, sendFakeAgentTurn } from "paseo-plugin-devkit";

const turn = runFakeAgentTurn(
  [
    { write: { path: "notes.md", content: "first\n" } },
    { bash: { command: "npm test", output: "ok", exitCode: 0 } },
    { say: "Done." },
  ],
  { cwd: workspace },
);
// waitFor polls until the probe returns something other than null (see the test linked below).
const [card] = await waitFor(() => {
  const rows = pluginRows(agentTimeline(turn.agentId), "turn-summary");
  return rows.length ? rows : null;
});
expect(card).toMatchObject({ data: { outcome: "completed", files: [join(workspace, "notes.md")], commands: ["npm test"] } });

// A chat-only turn gets no card.
sendFakeAgentTurn(turn.agentId, [{ say: "just chatting" }]);
```

The devkit's
[`test/create-e2e.test.ts`](https://github.com/nkwib/paseo-plugin-devkit/blob/main/test/create-e2e.test.ts) runs
this against a dev daemon it starts and stops itself, with `waitFor` and a failing turn.

<Callout kind="tip" title="Real agents">

The fake agent emits the canonical `write`, `edit` and `shell` items that Paseo maps real tools onto. Real adapters
can differ in the details, so run a hook once with a real agent before you ship it.

</Callout>
